<summary>💡 Fix Suggestion</summary>

**Suggestion:** After computing the clamped result, add a guard to ensure it never exceeds the absolute value of the original `delta`. When `sfAssetsTotal` sits mid-grid (>16 significant digits), rounding both endpoints under the same mode can produce a difference larger than the input. Cap the result with a simple comparison:

```cpp
    auto clamped = delta.negative() ? totalBefore - totalAfter : totalAfter - totalBefore;
    // Guard: rounding must never amplify the delta beyond the original magnitude.
    STAmount absDelta = delta;
    if (absDelta.negative())
        absDelta.negate();
    return clamped > absDelta ? absDelta : clamped;
```

This ensures the function's postcondition (result ≤ |delta|) always holds, even at mid-grid boundary values.

